# REMATCH — environment. Copy to `.env`; every line is optional.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Read by Node itself (`--env-file-if-exists=.env`) in both `pnpm dev:server` and
# `pnpm eval:agents`, so the demo and the eval cannot end up on different models.
# There is no `dotenv` dependency and a missing `.env` is a log line, not a crash.
#
# The defaults below are the **local-first** ones: nothing here spends money, and the
# game is fully playable as shipped (spec AC 1). The full table is in `README.md`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the model

# `none` forces fallback-only mode even if a key is present — the documented setting
# for local development, and the default in this file on purpose.
#
# What you still get with `none`: the whole game, all four interlude beats, and the
# pre-approved fallback pool, with the Analysis beat saying in as many words that no
# model ran. What you also still get, and what the demo video uses: a **real recorded
# run** of the model, replayed from disk for free —
#
#   pnpm dev, then open 'http://localhost:5173/?agent=recorded&autostart=1'
#
# Set this to `openai`, `anthropic`, or `auto` only when you actually intend to spend.
REMATCH_PROVIDER=none

# Credentials. Uncomment one — and remember that `REMATCH_PROVIDER=none` above still
# wins, which is the point: the off switch does not require deleting your key.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=...

# Per-agent models. Defaults are the chosen vendor's own (`gpt-5.4-mini` for OpenAI,
# `claude-sonnet-5` for Anthropic).
# REMATCH_MODEL=
# REMATCH_ANALYST_MODEL=
# REMATCH_CODER_MODEL=
# REMATCH_REASONING_EFFORT=low        # OpenAI only: minimal|low|medium|high|none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spend guards
#
# Added 2026-09-04, after eleven eval runs in one evening exhausted the account's
# credit (`docs/AI-DEV-LOG.md`). Both are on by default; neither needs configuring.

# Global cap on rewrites the server will pay for, per UTC day. Past it the server
# serves fallback-only for the rest of the day and `/api/health` reports
# `spendGuard: "capped"`. `0` means never spend — a good setting for a public deploy.
# This is NOT the per-IP rate limit (6 per 10 min), which is a different control for a
# different problem; see `packages/server/src/spendGuard.ts`.
# REMATCH_MAX_REWRITES_PER_DAY=50

# `pnpm eval:agents` refuses to run without this, printing the worst-case model-call
# count first (~250 for a default invocation). Deliberately NOT set here: a variable
# that has to be typed at the call site cannot be silently inherited from a file.
#
#   REMATCH_ALLOW_SPEND=1 pnpm eval:agents

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the loop

# REMATCH_CANDIDATES=3                # files the Coder writes per attempt
# REMATCH_DEADLINE_MS=40000           # loop deadline, inside AC 5's 45 s
# REMATCH_MATCHES=200                 # Gate 3 matches per attempt (spec §6.2)
# REMATCH_WORKERS=                    # Gate 3 threads, default availableParallelism()-1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- serving

# PORT=8787
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# REMATCH_ORIGIN=                     # extra allowed CORS origins, comma-separated
# REMATCH_ARTIFACT_DIR=               # event logs, default artifacts/server/
# VITE_API_BASE=                      # point the web bundle at a server elsewhere
